      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T23:25:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Makes sense, let\u0027s unify them. Though I\u0027m inclined towards SHARED_BORROWED rather than SHARED_OWNED, since pkvm_host_use_dma() already happens to use it, on ARM as well. And conceptually I think SHARED_OWNED would be as much a trick as SHARED_BORROWED is, since in pkvm_host_use_dma() the host doesn\u0027t actually share MMIO pages with the hypervisor or anyone else, i.e. they don\u0027t get mapped in the hypervisor\u0027s or anyone else\u0027s page tables.\n\n\u003e in pkvm_host_use_dma() we should avoid overwriting ramoops\u0027s WB memtype with host_mmu_pte_prot(true, true) (UC) if an already-shared page is skipped in the check loop.\n\nHmm... in such case it would be the host that hurts itself by requesting use_dma for a region that overlaps with ramoops? So I\u0027m not sure it\u0027s worth complicating the logic in pkvm_host_use_dma() for such a corner case.\n\nIn fact, perhaps a bigger potential problem is that we blindly map _any_ host\u0027s MMIO/reserved memory as UC, regardless of what memory type the host wants to use for it...",
      "parentUuid": "f36a8c75_528c71eb",
      "revId": "8c8e0065dbe1939ad538bc7066e43164aae75c3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
